6,Guinea-Bissau Creole Language (POV)... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/pov/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..II-qH4l1La_-go94lnqDXRcV5SHbHciUYoiQxmuAjYE,Guinea-Bissau Creole is a language of wider communication that originated in Guinea-Bissau. It is a Portuguese-based creole and used primarily as a second language.,Guinea-Bissau Creole,Creole
7,Guinea-Bissau Creole — Wikipedia Republished // WIKI 2,https://wiki2.org/en/Guinea-Bissau_Creole,"Guinea-Bissau Creole, also known as Kiriol or Crioulo, is a creole language whose lexicon derives mostly from Portuguese. It is spoken in Guinea Bissau, Senegal and The Gambia. It is also called by its native speakers as guinensi, kriyol, or portuguis.",Guinea-Bissau Creole,Creole
8,Guinea-Bissau: Official and widely spoken languages | TRAVEL.COM,https://travel.com/regions/africa/guinea-bissau/guinea-bissau-official-and-widely-spoken-languages/,"Guinea-Bissau Creole, or Kriol, is the heartbeat of daily life.Guinea-Bissau's festivals offer a unique window into the country's rich heritage, showcasing local traditions, music, and community spirit. As a travel destination, Guinea-Bissau is often overlooked",Guinea-Bissau Creole,Creole
9,Guinea-Bissau Creole - NYC Languages,https://languagemap.nyc/Explore/Language/Guinea-Bissau+Creole,"Guinea-Bissau Creole. Global speakers: 1,305,800.Guinea-Bissau Creole is a Portuguese-based creole spoken principally as a second language not only in the West African nation of Guinea-Bissau but in neighboring Senegal and The Gambia.",Guinea-Bissau Creole,Creole
